    "created_at": "2015-10-29T10:15:49Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-10-29T10:15:49Z",
    "body": "The spec has two concepts, the [form-associated elements](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/forms.html#form-associated-element) and the subcategory [listed elements](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/forms.html#category-listed). The `img` element is a form-associated element, but not in any of the subcategories.\n\nPer spec, [`HTMLFormControlsCollection`](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/infrastructure.html#the-htmlformcontrolscollection-interface) (`form.elements['foo']`) uses listed elements, while the [indexed for named property retrieval](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/forms.html#dom-form-nameditem) (`form['foo']`) uses first the listed elements, and then falls back to `img` elements and the past names map.\n\nHere are two ad-hoc test for these two code paths:\nhttp://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/3716\n\nIn Blink, both code paths return an image element. In Gecko and Edge, only the `form['foo']` variant does. The spec agrees with Gecko and Edge.\n\nBlink's `form['foo']` is implemented in terms of the `elements` collection internally, with only the past names fallback. If the `img` fallback were moved out to the same place, that would align more with the spec and other engines.\n\nWhat do you think, @tkent-google?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
