    "created_at": "2018-04-02T17:02:24Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-04-02T17:02:24Z",
    "body": "@TimvdLippe An `<img>` is a form-accociated element, and has a \"form owner\".  But it does not have a `form` property that allows script access to that \"form owner\".  The existence of the \"form owner\" is independent of whether there's a `form` property.\r\n\r\nIn particular, only \"listed elements\" in the sense of https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/forms.html#category-listed have a `form` property and allow an attribute named \"form\" to change what the form owner is.  And `<img>` is not in that list.\r\n\r\nSo that's the current state of things in the spec and at least in the Firefox implementation: `<img>` is form-associated, but not a \"listed element\".",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/377979276/reactions",
